-- title:
--   An equivariant archimedean type projector on K-finite functions
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a number field and let $tys$ be an archimedean type family for $F$, that is, data consisting of a natural number $tys.card\,w$ for each infinite place $w$ of $F$ together with, for each $i \in \mathrm{Fin}(tys.card\,w)$, an object `ArchRepAt F w`: a dimension $n$ and a representation $\rho$ of `rowIsometrySubgroup₀ w.Completion` on $\mathbb{C}^n$. The assertion is that there exists a $\mathbb{C}$-linear endomorphism $Q$ of the space of all functions $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_F) \to \mathbb{C}$, where $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_F)$ is `AdelicGL2 (𝓞 F) F`, with three properties. Write $A$ for `archCutSubmodule F tys`, the infimum over infinite places $w$ of the supremum over $i$ of the submodules `typeSubmodule (rowIsometryInclAt₀ F w) (tys.rep w i).ρ`, write $H$ for the supremum over infinite places $w$ of the ranges of the homomorphisms `rowIsometryInclAt₀ F w` (the subgroup of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_F)$ generated by their images), and for $\varphi$ a function write $S(\varphi)$ for the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the set of right translates $x \mapsto \varphi(xk)$ with $k \in H$. Then: (1) $Q\varphi = \varphi$ for every continuous $\varphi \in A$; (2) for every continuous $\varphi$ with $S(\varphi)$ finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{C}$, $Q\varphi$ lies in $A \sqcap S(\varphi)$; and (3) for every such $\varphi$ and every $k \in H$, $Q$ commutes with right translation by $k$, i.e. $Q(x \mapsto \varphi(xk)) = (x \mapsto (Q\varphi)(xk))$.
--
--   This is the existence of the isotypic projector onto a prescribed family of archimedean $K$-types: on continuous functions whose translates under the archimedean compact subgroup span a finite-dimensional space, $Q$ projects onto the part of prescribed type, equivariantly and without leaving the span of translates. It is used in the construction of the archimedean cut projector [`AutomorphicForm.exists_linearMap_archCutProjector`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.exists_linearMap_archCutProjector) and in the bounds [`AutomorphicForm.CuspidalConstituent.iSup_inf_levelInvariantSubmodule_inf_archCutSubmodule_le`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.CuspidalConstituent.iSup_inf_levelInvariantSubmodule_inf_archCutSubmodule_le) and its principal-level variant.
